          "thread": "Montenegro extradition tug-of-war",
          "why": "The back-and-forth between US and South Korean extradition requests — including allegations that Do Kwon was traded as a diplomatic chip for airport control — made this feel like a geopolitical thriller, not a legal proceeding."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Prison crypto wallet access",
          "why": "Authorities taking 72 days to seize his crypto login details — during which payments were allegedly made — exposed a concrete gap between legal custody and actual asset control."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "SEC settlement and fine scale",
          "why": "A $4.47B settlement that made up nearly all of the SEC's record 2024 enforcement total gave readers a measurable yardstick for the collapse's institutional damage."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Jump Trading institutional role",
          "why": "Jump Crypto's alleged misrepresentation of TerraUSD's stability — and its president invoking the Fifth Amendment — implicated a major market maker and widened the fraud narrative beyond Do Kwon alone."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Guilty plea and 15-year sentence",
          "why": "The pivot from not-guilty to guilty plea, culminating in a 15-year sentence delivered against a backdrop of victim letters describing suicides and bankruptcies, gave readers a rare moment of resolution in a years-long saga."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Human cost and victim impact",
          "why": "Testimonies of suicides, destroyed families, and lost life savings from a $40B collapse shifted the story from regulatory abstraction to documented human harm."
        }
      ]
